# Virtual environments. Anchored to the repository root on purpose: unanchored "env/"
# also matched data/Human_immunodeficiency_virus_1/env/, the HIV-1 envelope gene directory,
# which is why that directory was missing from clones (Reviewer #2, software comment 2).
/venv/
/env/
/ENV/
/env.bak/
/venv.bak/

# Jupyter Notebook
.ipynb_checkpoints
*.ipynb_checkpoints/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Project specific
# Temporary output files
*.xlsx
!examples/outputs/*.xlsx
# The supplementary workbooks moved out of notebooks/ but this exception did not follow them,
# so a new S-numbered table dropped into supplementary/ was ignored without a word. The twelve
# already tracked survived only because tracked files ignore .gitignore. Same failure as R2-S2.
!supplementary/S*_Table.*
!notebooks/S*_Table.xlsx

# Results directories
data/*/results/
# Generated PDF reports (produced by `python main.py --report N`)
*_report.pdf
# The toy report is the one output the README describes that a reader cannot see without
# installing the project, and it answers the report request of comment 4.5. Regenerate it
# with: python main.py data/toy/config.yaml --report 12
!data/toy/toy_report.pdf
# Broad rule aimed at generated result files. It also silently excluded the substitution
# matrices, which left MIYATA_EVO.pkl as the only matrix present in a clone, so they are
# re-included explicitly below.
*.json
!data/*/reference/*.json
!src/substitution_matrices/*.json
# The cached UniProt entries the protein component is computed from, one per analysed gene.
# Only the toy's was kept until 30 July 2026, which made the quick start work offline from a
# clone but left the published scores dependent on the service being reachable at the moment
# someone tries to reproduce them. On 29 July a run made while offline scored every SARS-CoV-2
# protein at zero, so the loader now raises rather than returning a value; committing the
# records means it has no reason to. That reason has only grown: UniProt now serves later
# versions than the ones the published scores were computed from, so the service no longer
# reproduces them at all.
#
# Listed one by one rather than with a wildcard. The wildcard let an unreferenced entry sit
# here unnoticed: P16849, which is UL33 and not one of the eleven analysed genes, was carried
# for months. Each file below is the exact byte-for-byte copy deposited on Zenodo and verified
# against the SHA-256 in results/protein_score_validation/protein_score_provenance.csv.
!src/uniprot/index.json
!src/uniprot/P04578.json
!src/uniprot/P04585.json
!src/uniprot/P04591.json
!src/uniprot/P06473.json
!src/uniprot/P0DTC2.json
!src/uniprot/P0DTC4.json
!src/uniprot/P0DTC5.json
!src/uniprot/P0DTC9.json
!src/uniprot/P0DTD1.json
!src/uniprot/P16795.json
!src/uniprot/P69332.json
# Two more the broad rule caught, both read at startup rather than produced for a reader: the
# benchmark configuration the statistics and the overlap analysis are computed against, and the
# descriptive ranking summary S7 Table and the cross-check both open. A clone received the code
# that reads them and not the files, so the cross-check could not run from a fresh clone.
!notebooks/discriminative_score_validation_results/config.json
!results/statistical_comparison/descriptive_mean_ranks_summary.json
# The compiled per-position output of the pipeline, one file per analysed gene. The crosscheck
# reads them to verify S10 to S12 cell by cell, the indel statistics, the windowing grid and the
# twenty-six KSS values the concordance quotes, and `generate_kss_figure.ipynb` writes the three
# workbooks and Figure 3 from them. Ignored until 29 August 2026, which meant the harness stopped
# at 378 checks of 764 on a fresh clone, on FileNotFoundError, while Data availability promised
# "the scripts that reproduce every reported result". They are derived aggregates, scores and
# class counts per position: no sequence, no accession, no path. 6.6 MB for the twelve.
!data/*/*/results/*_compiled_results.json

# Logs
*.log

# Sequence data (too large for GitHub, see README for download instructions)
*.fasta
# Exception: the 16-sequence toy for the quick-start ships with the repository.
!data/toy/US28/sequences.fasta

# Manuscript: track the sources so revisions are recoverable, keep the heavy
# binaries (compiled PDFs, Word exports, archives, reference articles) out.
manuscript/**
!manuscript/*.tex
# Generated by build_diff.ps1 from the submitted and the revised sources. Committing it would
# ship a copy that goes stale on the next edit of either one.
manuscript/diff_vs_submitted.tex
!manuscript/*.bib
!manuscript/*.bst
!manuscript/*.md
!manuscript/submitted/
!manuscript/submitted/*.tex
!manuscript/*.ps1
!manuscript/figures/
# The three figures the manuscript includes. They were unversioned, so a fresh clone could not
# compile it, and a change to one of them could not travel with the change that caused it.
!manuscript/figures/KSS_workflow.png
!manuscript/figures/discriminative_validation_by_dataset.png
!manuscript/figures/KSS_validation.png
!manuscript/figures/sources/
!manuscript/figures/sources/*.drawio
!manuscript/archive/
!manuscript/archive/README.md
# Revision tracking. Without these the broad rule above silently swallows the documents a
# future session needs to reorient itself, which is the same trap that hid data/HIV-1/env
# and the substitution matrices from clones.
!manuscript/revision/
!manuscript/revision/*.md
!manuscript/revision/*.txt
manuscript/archive/overleaf_snapshots/extracted/
notebooks/vog_data/
# The COV2Var download, kept under data/external/ with the other external inputs. Only the
# seven files the analysis reads are retained; the other five, 138 MB of them, were never
# opened by anything. scripts/external_inputs.py verifies the checksums before reading.
data/external/COV2Var/

# Upstream source files that are not ours, cached locally rather than redistributed. The two
# complete sources carry GPL notices, VTML200 travels inside the GPL-licensed spaln
# distribution, FLAVI comes from a repository that publishes no licence at all, and wag.dat is
# the authors' own EBI file with no licence statement. build_added_matrices.py and
# build_viral_matrices.py download them and verify their SHA-256 digests before use.
/scripts/added_matrix_sources/iqtree_modelprotein.cpp
/scripts/added_matrix_sources/raxml_models.c
/scripts/added_matrix_sources/VTML200_spaln.txt
/scripts/added_matrix_sources/wag.dat
/scripts/added_matrix_sources/FLAVI_authors.PAML

# Sorties de travail temporaires: rendus de pages, apercus de figures.
tmp/

# Per-gene partials of the cost measurement. --merge assembles them into
# computational_cost.csv, which is the published table; they are kept on disk so one gene can be
# remeasured and merged again without rerunning the other ten, but nothing reads them after that.
results/computational_cost/computational_cost_*.csv
